From: cloud-comms-engine <engine@diegonmarcos.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] rebrand: Cloud Matrix app name + applicationId, add NOTICE

Element X declares both its identity strings in one place, so the rebrand is
two constants rather than a sweep:

  APPLICATION_ID   io.element.android.x -> com.diegonmarcos.comms.matrix
  APPLICATION_NAME "Element X"          -> "Cloud Matrix"

applicationId matters beyond naming: forks.matrix.app_id already says
com.diegonmarcos.comms.matrix, and until this change a from-source build
produced upstream's id instead - so the APK could not take over from the
resigned stock build, and signature-level constellation IPC keyed on our id
would not have matched it.

NOTICE.md elects AGPL-3.0-only (upstream is dual-licensed AGPL-3.0-only OR
LicenseRef-Element-Commercial), disclaims the Element trademarks, and records
that the launcher artwork in appicon/element/ has NOT yet been replaced.

NOTE: this tree is VENDORED (materialize-fork's no-.git path), so this file is
a historical record - the change is already applied in the committed source.
It is kept so the delta from upstream v26.06.2 stays readable.
---
 plugins/src/main/kotlin/config/BuildTimeConfig.kt | 4 ++--
 NOTICE.md                                         | new
 2 files changed

diff --git a/plugins/src/main/kotlin/config/BuildTimeConfig.kt b/plugins/src/main/kotlin/config/BuildTimeConfig.kt
--- a/plugins/src/main/kotlin/config/BuildTimeConfig.kt
+++ b/plugins/src/main/kotlin/config/BuildTimeConfig.kt
@@ -10,8 +10,8 @@ package config

 object BuildTimeConfig {
-    const val APPLICATION_ID = "io.element.android.x"
-    const val APPLICATION_NAME = "Element X"
+    const val APPLICATION_ID = "com.diegonmarcos.comms.matrix"
+    const val APPLICATION_NAME = "Cloud Matrix"
     const val GOOGLE_APP_ID_RELEASE = "1:912726360885:android:d097de99a4c23d2700427c"
